-- Whether the allowance is paid depends on `resident`, but how much depends
-- on `income`, which no condition reads. The report tries `income` at one
-- value, so it says which input that is rather than let one printed answer
-- stand for every income.
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER
      resident IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `allowance` IS
  IF resident THEN income TIMES 0.1 ELSE 0
